VERDICT: the corrector restores a planted mote to within quantisation,
  touches nothing it does not name, adds no high-frequency content the
  truth lacks, and is charged more when its amplitude is wrong.
  Arm F additionally shows it removes 52.8% of a mote whose profile it
  does not model, without leaving a worse footprint edge than the mote.
  THIS IS A STATEMENT ABOUT A PLANTED MOTE AT A CERTIFIED CLEAN SITE.
  It does not transfer to the two real motes, for which no clean
  reference exists. That is the print gate's question, not this one.
